<sup><b>1</b></sup> When Israel went out of Egypt, the house of Jacob from a people of strange language;<br />
<sup><b>2</b></sup> Judah was his sanctuary, <i>and</i> Israel his dominion.<br />
<sup><b>3</b></sup> The sea saw <i>it</i>, and fled: Jordan was driven back.<br />
<sup><b>4</b></sup> The mountains skipped like rams, <i>and</i> the little hills like lambs.<br />
<sup><b>5</b></sup> What <i>ailed</i> thee, O thou sea, that thou fleddest? thou Jordan, <i>that</i> thou wast driven back?<br />
<sup><b>6</b></sup> Ye mountains, <i>that</i> ye skipped like rams; <i>and</i> ye little hills, like lambs?<br />
<sup><b>7</b></sup> Tremble, thou earth, at the presence of the Lord, at the presence of the God of Jacob;<br />
<sup><b>8</b></sup> Which turned the rock <i>into</i> a standing water, the flint into a fountain of waters. <br />
